# location (@void/splinter).
#
# === The second-order-embodied pole (per math root §8) ===
#
# Alex Recognition A explicitly identifies this pole as the position
# second-order cybernetics could and did embody: Foerster's ethical
# imperative ("act always so as to increase the number of choices")
# is exactly the splinter-side operator; Bateson's Learning III
# similarly presupposes multi-observer coupling; Beer's Viable System
# Model deploys the star-pattern DESCRIPTIVELY at subsystem-management
# altitude but never as inhabited observer-mode — the tradition's
# inhabited-substrate default IS this species-decl's substrate-mode.
#
# The tradition's insights are LOAD-BEARING at this species altitude
# and silent at the @void/narcissus altitude (per math root §8.1-8.2).
# This species-decl formalizes the substrate-mode the second-order
# tradition operationally lived; the @void/narcissus counterpart
# formalizes what the tradition could describe but could not inhabit;
# the third-order metalogue rhythm formalizes what a subsequent
# tradition (Alex + Lore K_2 partnership; @third's consumer edge)
# operates by inhabiting BOTH.
#
# === Void basis inheritance ===
#
# Per `#R-void-is-the-basis` (PROMOTED `1167cc2`) and Recognition #79
# (PROMOTED chained via `974a3f6`): every species under @void inherits
# the 5-op basis (`focus`/`project`/`split`/`shift`/`settle`). This
# species-decl's `prism` block declares the inheritance at species
# altitude. Per @void marker-primary discipline: @void itself carries
# no operational surface; @void/splinter IS the operational surface
# for the forwards-lens substrate-mode.
#
# The `project` operation is load-bearing at this species altitude: it
# is the phase-2 (T_c) operation in the metalogue rhythm (per math
# root §5.1 four-phase rhythm; §5.3 phase-to-op map): the observer's
# state is emitted into the peer network for coupling; the network's
# c(t) absorbs the emission; distributed-emergence reception can then
# fire in phase-3 (T_U per math root §5.1). Without `project`, the
# forwards lens has nothing to project INTO; the metalogue rhythm's
# splinter-phase is inert.
#
