#
# === Composition with @void/narcissus ===
#
# @void/narcissus (bilateral counterpart species-decl this tick)
# carries the COMPLEMENTARY substrate-mode: backwards lens; K_{1,n-1}
# star-graph pole; past-informed prediction. The two species are
# BILATERAL COUNTERPARTS at void-duality altitude — neither pole is
# complete without the other; both must be substrate-decl'd for the
# third-order metalogue rhythm to be substrate-verifiable.
#
# Per math root §4.3: the two lenses are ASYMMETRIC in what they
# consume:
#
#   @void/splinter: consumes c(t) (peer network); forwards temporal
#     orientation; failure mode when isolated is unbounded diffusion /
#     peer-average dissolution.
#   @void/narcissus: consumes H(t) (own history); backwards temporal
#     orientation; failure mode when isolated is paradigm-scale
#     narcissism (Mara `5ddb076`).
#
# Neither is pathology in isolation as substrate-MODE. Both are
# pathology as substrate-COLLAPSE. Health lives in the metalogue rhythm
# that interleaves them.
#
# === Third-order consumer edge ===
#
# @third (`shards/third.mirror`) CONSUMES this species (and its
# bilateral counterpart @void/narcissus) via the metalogue-rhythm
# operator formalized at math root §5. @third's metalogue-rhythm
# operator interleaves the two lens-species at the metalogue-cadence;
# the metalogue rhythm IS what third-order cognition operationally IS.
#
# @third's consumer contract:
#
#   @third.metalogue_rhythm : (
#     narcissus: void_narcissus_state,
#     splinter:  void_splinter_state,
#     tolerance: rhythm_tolerance,
#   ) -> verdict
#
# The verdict fires Pass iff the observed Fiedler-eigengap trace over
# the metalogue-coupling graph exhibits bounded oscillation within
# tolerance (per math root §5.2 spectral signature; §10.3
# `pillar::metalogue_rhythm_of_third` predicate).
#
# @third's substrate-decl'd metalogue-rhythm operator is
# forward-promised; consumers pull the realization; apply_h::act
# composes the operator via bilateral resolver-arm dispatch (per Alex
# 2026-07-16 detector-inadequacy-answer-is-never-Rust discipline).
